{
  "title": "Duration",
  "description": "A length of time that the holder may read but not change. The type every duration the engine hands out is declared as - the frame delta, the fixed step, a clock's elapsed time, the canonical constants on Time. Each of those is a shared instance the engine keeps mutating, so a caller that needs a duration of its own copies it into one: `Time.fromMilliseconds(delta.milliseconds)`. Time implements it. Take a `Time` instead where the callee is meant to write.",
